 ## Operating characteristics
-- **Time Complexity:** The naive summation approach is $O(N N_\theta N_\rho)$, which simplifies to $O(N^2)$ if $N_\theta, N_\rho \propto \sqrt{N}$ [S3, unofficial]. With optimized mapping of pixels to contributing projection lines, it can reach $O(N \log N)$ [S3, unofficial]. The FFT-based filtering adds $O(N_\rho \log N_\rho)$ per angle.
-- **Memory Complexity:** Requires storage for the sinogram, the filtered sinogram, and the output image. The FFT padding increases the radial dimension slightly.
